{"notes":["SECURITY REVIEW alex-security (muse-spark-1.2-contributor) — analysis-only, scope anvil-cli/sto:local-deploy-cli #8 in-review 971d6be, branch feat/sto-local-deploy-cli commit 94f2e4c worktree ../worktrees/feat-sto-local-deploy-cli. Diff: cmd/deploy.go 521L + cmd/deploy_test.go 528L + cmd/root.go group. Reuses internal/artifact.Package/VerifyArtifact + internal/output (AppError/envelope v1/PlainStepReporter) per spikes/local-deploy-ux. Threats reviewed: secret leakage via logs/temp paths/error messages/JSON vs human (--json), DEPLOY_SSH_KEY handling (future), host-key verification bypass (deferred). OWASP Top10, ASVS, secret mgmt, temp disclosure, error handling.","FINDINGS BY SEVERITY — 0 BLOCKING, 2 MEDIUM, 3 LOW, 2 INFO — overall VERDICT: APPROVE (no gate). No verified secret leak in this slice; JSON human parity PASS.","[MEDIUM][NON-BLOCKING] F1 Missing secret-redaction wrapper in deploy error paths — cmd/deploy.go:157-232 all AppError Reason use raw err.Error() without RedactSecrets/SanitizeLogLine. Spike spikes/local-deploy-ux/errors.go ClassifiedError uses redactErr() and SanitizeTarget, deployment_upload.go redacts DEPLOY_SSH_KEY; deploy lacks parity. Current slice has no DEPLOY_SSH_KEY read so not exploitable now, but any future transport error that embeds id_rsa/.pem/key path or DEPLOY_SSH_KEY value will leak verbatim to stderr and JSON error envelope (ReportError writes e.Error() = Message+Err to JSON error field). Evidence: grep -n Redact in cmd/deploy.go = 0 hits; TestDeploy_NoSecretLeakInErrors only asserts DEPLOY_SSH_KEY not in current outputs. Mitigation (pragmatic, ~5m): add func redactDeployErr(error) string wrapping spikes RedactSecrets logic — if lower contains deploy_ssh_key/begin open/private or '/' + key/id_rsa/id_ed25519/.pem return ***REDACTED*** or base+[REDACTED_PATH]; apply to every Reason/Err string before AppError construction and to WriteJSONError path. Wire for next work item transport; add test with env DEPLOY_SSH_KEY=supersecret assert output contains ***REDACTED*** not raw value.","[MEDIUM][NON-BLOCKING] F2 Temp artifact lifetime \u0026 permission disclosure — cmd/deploy.go:171 MkdirTemp(\"anvil-deploy-*\") with comment 'Do not remove, OS-managed' leaks tar.gz containing filtered project content to /tmp indefinitely. On shared builder/host other local users can read it; human output correctly uses filepath.Base only (test asserts no /tmp leak) but JSON data.artifact_path is absolute /tmp/.../artifact.tar.gz by design for machine consumption. Disk-fill DoS possible with repeated deploy. Evidence: ls shows no cleanup, no defer os.RemoveAll. Mitigation: add defer cleanup after success/failure unless --keep-artifact flag (opt-in for debugging), ensure MkdirTemp 0700 (Go does 0700 but verify on host umask), document retention in help Long; add t.Cleanup in tests already uses t.TempDir for isolation. Severity medium only on multi-tenant hosts; single-dev low.","[LOW][NON-BLOCKING] F3 Target flag terminal injection — cmd/deploy.go:208 humanReporter.Start(fmt.Sprintf(\"Deploy --target %s\", target)) plus renderDeployHuman interpolates raw target into stdout without sanitization. If target contains \\n, \\r, or ANSI escapes (e.g. --target $'\\n[pwn]'), it can inject fake [PASS]/[FAIL] lines or cursor moves. Low exploit (local CLI, no privilege esc). Mitigation: use %q or SanitizeTarget = strings.TrimSpace + redact + limit to [a-z0-9_-] allowlist; add validation regex ^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9_-]{0,63}$ and reject with ExitCodeConfig. Also apply to error Message fmt.Sprintf(\"deploy to %q\") already uses %q — keep.","[LOW][NON-BLOCKING] F4 Absolute temp path in JSON envelope information disclosure — deploy.go:327 data[\"artifact_path\"]=result.ArtifactPath absolute. Human hides full path via Base, JSON intentionally exposes full path for automation (tests assert JSON has artifact_path). Not secret but leaks host filesystem layout (/tmp/anvil-deploy-XXXX) to logs/CI aggregators. Mitigation: document as intentional; consider returning only base or relative to project unless --json includes absolute for tooling — if so, advise consumers to not log JSON verbatim to external systems. No code change needed now; add note to help under Secrets are never printed.","[LOW][NON-BLOCKING] F5 Missing anvil.yaml server.targets[env] validation — spec says --target required and declared in server.targets (future); deploy.go:115-136 only checks empty and protected allowlist, never loads cfg.ServerTargets or validates unknown env. Arbitrary target names still build+verify success, masking misconfig that will fail at transport stage. Not auth bypass (no transport yet) but fail-open. Mitigation: defer to sto:local-deploy-config — when server.targets exists, add lookup and exit 2 'unknown target env' with list of known envs (use --json consistent). Reuse deployment.ReadSSHCredentials pattern for known error strings.","[INFO] F6 Host-key verification deferred — ACCEPTED. AC states deferred to config; deploy MVP performs build+verify only, no SSH transport, so no MITM exposure now. Existing deployment_upload.go already implements KnownHosts verification via deployment.WithKnownHosts (strict/accept-new, fail-closed on misconfig) and tests deployment_upload_knownhosts_test.go PASS. Risk is future integration forgetting to wire KnownHosts. Mitigation: add TODO comment in deploy.go linking to anvil-cli/adr:local-deploy-transport and require next work item to reuse deployment.SSHCredentials KnownHostsPath/Mode; add CI check that non-dry-run deploy calls deployment layer.","[INFO] F7 Checksum/verification-before-trust — POSITIVE. VerifyArtifact runs 6 checks (archive validity, manifest presence/content, project identity, checksum match, immutability) with two-phase safeExtractPath (ZipSlip protected, TD-001). Verify FAIL correctly exits 1 general with guidance, both human (print checks) and JSON (collectFailedChecks Reason). No TOCTOU observed. Keep gate enforced قبل install.","EVIDENCE: code inspection cmd/deploy.go all paths; internal/output error.go/json.go/exitcode.go + cmd/conventions.go ReportError/WriteJSON (JSON vs human branching correct, SilenceErrors true); internal/artifact/verification.go safeExtractPath + two-phase extract; internal/deployment/ssh_credentials.go KnownHosts strict default; spikes/local-deploy-ux/errors.go RedactSecrets vs deploy gap; tests go test ./cmd -run TestDeploy -count=1 PASS 13/13 + TestDeploy_NoSecretLeakInErrors PASS (human base only, no DEPLOY_SSH_KEY echo); manual grep 0 Redact hits in deploy; MkdirTemp leak observed; git diff 94f2e4c only deploy files.","MITIGATIONS PRIORITY: P1 (before transport) F1 add redactDeployErr wrapper + test with real secret value. P2 F2 add temp cleanup/--keep-artifact. P3 F3 sanitize/validate --target. F4/F5 docs + future validation. F6 gate next PR to require KnownHosts wiring. All without redesign, ~15m.","OPEN ISSUES \u0026 ASSUMPTIONS: No DEPLOY_SSH_KEY handling in this slice — future work must not read key from anvil.yaml, only env, and must chmod 0600 check. Assumes single-user dev host for temp risk; shared CI must enable cleanup. Assumes artifact filtering excludes .env/secret files via config.artifact include/exclude — verified via PackageOptions.","RECOMMENDED NEXT STEPS: 1) Apply P1 redaction helper before sto done. 2) Add cleanup flag. 3) Keep security test with DEPLOY_SSH_KEY=supersecret asserting ***REDACTED*** in both human and JSON error. 4) Next work item must import deployment layer with KnownHosts verification and redact wrapper. 5) Publish this note via eka publish."],"role":"review","verdict":"approve"}